{"title":"Career Roadmap · Public Health Nutritionist","role":"Public Health Nutritionist","summary":"A Public Health Nutritionist works at the population level to prevent malnutrition, micronutrient deficiencies, obesity, diet-related diseases, and other nutrition-related public-health problems. Unlike a Clinical Dietitian, who primarily works with individual patients, a Public Health Nutritionist focuses on communities, populations, programs, policy, surveillance, nutrition education, and program evaluation.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Public Health Nutritionist works at the population level to prevent malnutrition, micronutrient deficiencies, obesity, diet-related diseases, and other nutrition-related public-health problems. Unlike a Clinical Dietitian, who primarily works with individual patients, a Public Health Nutritionist focuses on communities, populations, programs, policy, surveillance, nutrition education, and program evaluation."},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the strongest direct academic pathway within the supplied category is a recognized B.Sc/B.Sc (Hons.) Nutrition & Dietetics, Food & Nutrition, Clinical Nutrition & Dietetics, or Public Health Nutrition-related program. Generic BPT, BOT, or BMLT degrees do not automatically qualify someone as a Public Health Nutritionist."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical work environments include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government health programs"},{"text":"Public-health departments"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"International development organizations"},{"text":"Nutrition foundations"},{"text":"Community-health programs"},{"text":"Research institutions"},{"text":"Maternal and child-health programs"},{"text":"School nutrition programs"},{"text":"Food-security initiatives"},{"text":"Healthcare organizations"},{"text":"Public-health consulting"}]}]},{"heading":"Career H